From ee9215ab23c6d56209c8703dd21fc7fd63fdb4d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Brian S. Park" <brianspark@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:26:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cuda: fuse the KV rotation FWHT into rms_norm_mul_rope

With a quantized KV cache, Q and K each go RMS_NORM, MUL, ROPE, RESHAPE,
Hadamard MUL_MAT (run as fwht_cuda): two launches per tensor.  Run the
FWHT in the fused rope kernel instead: the roped row goes through shared
memory into the same in-warp FWHT code (now a helper in fwht.cuh, used by
fwht_cuda too, so both compile under the same contraction mode).

The rotation output may alias the norm input exactly (the allocator
reuses the dead projection); each block reads its row of x before a
barrier and only then writes the same row of dst, so that alias is
allowed.  GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_ROPE_FWHT turns the fusion off.
Bit-identical output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
